    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "Serialization formats\nFor serializing the scraped data, the feed exports use the [Item exporters](exporters.html#topics-exporters). These formats are supported out of the box:",
        "text_sha256": "29e4082847c071d090fa001560b8a578ade9c7b47f36bf75ded1bab436bf8deb",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 874,
            "end": 1050,
            "line_start": 22,
            "line_end": 24
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "- JSON\n- JSON lines\n- CSV\n- XML",
        "text_sha256": "0606f86a416f29f8105ccf6ac4e0bb57a11439bbbc90c45d4010c029cdae00b2",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 1052,
            "end": 1083,
            "line_start": 26,
            "line_end": 29
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "But you can also extend the supported format through the\n`FEED_EXPORTERS` setting.",
        "text_sha256": "ee6b57f81c52766721732b6ada17acec9f826062c3b72edaa7b19f7091b042fb",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 1085,
            "end": 1167,
            "line_start": 31,
            "line_end": 32
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "http": 4,
    "window_ordinal": 3,
    "window_id": "b6ecb7c9-1f7e-55c3-a661-d880cadf5468",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "But you can also extend the supported format through the\n`FEED_EXPORTERS` setting.",
        "text_sha256": "ee6b57f81c52766721732b6ada17acec9f826062c3b72edaa7b19f7091b042fb",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 1085,
            "end": 1167,
            "line_start": 31,
            "line_end": 32
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "JSON\n- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `json`\n- Exporter used: [`JsonItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.JsonItemExporter)\n- See [this warning](exporters.html#json-with-large-data) if you’re using JSON with\nlarge feeds.",
        "text_sha256": "80b758770346a8d037ad4118a5b5a6fc0258654026ebe16ed03b8506037e3b7c",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 1173,
            "end": 1423,
            "line_start": 34,
            "line_end": 39
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "JSON lines\n- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `jsonlines`\n- Exporter used: [`JsonLinesItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.JsonLinesItemExporter)",
        "text_sha256": "f24e073cd5bdf283d554b5309e724993b466bffed53d51eda0ab1ada15542069",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 1429,
            "end": 1603,
            "line_start": 41,
            "line_end": 44
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "CSV\n- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `csv`\n- Exporter used: [`CsvItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.CsvItemExporter)\n- To specify columns to export, their order and their column names, use\n`FEED_EXPORT_FIELDS`. Other feed exporters can also use this\noption, but it is important for CSV because unlike many other export\nformats CSV uses a fixed header.",
        "text_sha256": "b75a3613d7e5f93f20cc05b441cf06fb143cd0fbfbeb535755a6b1791e9c6b39",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 1609,
            "end": 1993,
            "line_start": 46,
            "line_end": 53
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "XML\n- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `xml`\n- Exporter used: [`XmlItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.XmlItemExporter)",
        "text_sha256": "851f49d350eeb5a75b74afffec2544a12c8e40756f21df8a118fc26c5e88680b",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 1999,
            "end": 2148,
            "line_start": 55,
            "line_end": 58
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Pickle\n- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `pickle`\n- Exporter used: [`PickleItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.PickleItemExporter)",
        "text_sha256": "6cc7708d68e04ab8441a50c6e211951be0261363bee82f224de33b67dd48ca19",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 2154,
            "end": 2315,
            "line_start": 60,
            "line_end": 63
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Marshal\n- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `marshal`\n- Exporter used: [`MarshalItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.MarshalItemExporter)",
        "text_sha256": "7a3a662cffab4cafe01e40f8727e95ad7fecccc1147c50463752e9cb23afc3b5",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 2321,
            "end": 2486,
            "line_start": 65,
            "line_end": 68
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Storages\nWhen using the feed exports you define where to store the feed using one or multiple [URIs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniform_Resource_Identifier)\n(through the `FEEDS` setting). The feed exports supports multiple\nstorage backend types which are defined by the URI scheme.",
        "text_sha256": "8a618de8f3b509f88780709cf57d34f728ff8642ae3929f764cc826f0ada2f61",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 2491,
            "end": 2776,
            "line_start": 70,
            "line_end": 74
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "http": 5,
    "window_ordinal": 4,
    "window_id": "f74b9620-caf0-5e33-8904-cee96b13b4e1",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "The storages backends supported out of the box are:",
        "text_sha256": "945442de36fee87525385d03cc23b3baec629038c0c02d8146101fb3e88d0ae7",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 2778,
            "end": 2829,
            "line_start": 76,
            "line_end": 76
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "- Local filesystem\n- FTP\n- S3 (requires [boto3](https://github.com/boto/boto3))\n- Google Cloud Storage (GCS) (requires [google-cloud-storage](https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/reference/libraries#client-libraries-install-python))\n- Standard output",
        "text_sha256": "fb291e16c65e958e0fb0a64c45ee0b9217a6ffd57bd8191258d0671587e13f4c",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 2831,
            "end": 3082,
            "line_start": 78,
            "line_end": 82
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Some storage backends may be unavailable if the required external libraries are\nnot available. For example, the S3 backend is only available if the [boto3](https://github.com/boto/boto3)\nlibrary is installed.",
        "text_sha256": "5775baf32cc962f94c69800e8bf73f396c38061f656451dc864162f08ba7cc4a",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 3084,
            "end": 3292,
            "line_start": 84,
            "line_end": 86
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "http": 6,
    "window_ordinal": 5,
    "window_id": "fc691e95-7c27-5554-9c50-d6da77571a8c",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "Storage URI parameters\nThe storage URI can also contain parameters that get replaced when the feed is\nbeing created. These parameters are:",
        "text_sha256": "55bceef8232e17f1e31ee3e5df69dbee25974d2982f7bfadfc2efe2ca0cd8f2c",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 3297,
            "end": 3436,
            "line_start": 88,
            "line_end": 91
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "- `%(time)s` - gets replaced by a timestamp when the feed is being created\n- `%(name)s` - gets replaced by the spider name",
        "text_sha256": "3686d9197ebded9fa7e5625946c8607477eebde177e3df8cd5a7f34193094f16",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 3438,
            "end": 3560,
            "line_start": 93,
            "line_end": 94
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Any other named parameter gets replaced by the spider attribute of the same\nname. For example, `%(site_id)s` would get replaced by the `spider.site_id`\nattribute the moment the feed is being created.",
        "text_sha256": "cf09812c859f6a7c81f78dca00a82e459c23e07c35189a1b27d734aa07659958",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 3562,
            "end": 3761,
            "line_start": 96,
            "line_end": 98
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "http": 7,
    "window_ordinal": 6,
    "window_id": "069686c1-495e-50cd-ba21-ffb1abf3b6e0",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "Here are some examples to illustrate:",
        "text_sha256": "a592f8e7cfef004daab9661a276ed86a2d8ad85d98335a4572edaebd7d5c1d1e",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 3763,
            "end": 3800,
            "line_start": 100,
            "line_end": 100
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "- Store in FTP using one directory per spider:\n  - `ftp://user:password@ftp.example.com/scraping/feeds/%(name)s/%(time)s.json`\n- Store in S3 using one directory per spider:\n  - `s3://mybucket/scraping/feeds/%(name)s/%(time)s.json`",
        "text_sha256": "db14331d8f2061c3daaf494e9ddd9e6f4ed1c9a82d813e96276f98df42af1691",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 3802,
            "end": 4032,
            "line_start": 102,
            "line_end": 105
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "[Spider arguments](spiders.html#spiderargs) become spider attributes, hence\nthey can also be used as storage URI parameters.",
        "text_sha256": "b552caf606ff5780589219c30379cb833ce9fb24fd5bf504b9144f2800f0e86e",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 4034,
            "end": 4158,
            "line_start": 107,
            "line_end": 108
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "http": 8,
    "window_ordinal": 7,
    "window_id": "3921ea38-0e22-51b6-85cd-41cc7324eca4",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "Local filesystem\nThe feeds are stored in the local filesystem.",
        "text_sha256": "a7f9f9b19811735a10f27e7aa4c4e6c22f595c5f12d204e4de2f675e3d4fd323",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 4185,
            "end": 4248,
            "line_start": 112,
            "line_end": 114
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "- URI scheme: `file`\n- Example URI: `file:///tmp/export.csv`\n- Required external libraries: none",
        "text_sha256": "52c8f16af38f3dbcdf13250e5d93471da2a0f72018598dce3d7995488dd6379c",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 4250,
            "end": 4346,
            "line_start": 116,
            "line_end": 118
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Note that for the local filesystem storage (only) you can omit the scheme if\nyou specify an absolute path like `/tmp/export.csv` (Unix systems only).\nAlternatively you can also use a [`pathlib.Path`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.Path) object.",
        "text_sha256": "a42dd78d60f59d54e9461566930d191239f3cfb52114df55a4bd1be0a348af4e",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 4348,
            "end": 4616,
            "line_start": 120,
            "line_end": 122
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "http": 9,
    "window_ordinal": 8,
    "window_id": "1fcfbdc7-b19d-5135-934b-672052592609",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "FTP\nThe feeds are stored in a FTP server.",
        "text_sha256": "52013b3501b21705e763875e2223937ddf0e3c231974c508322ae2b6ed34ef53",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 4622,
            "end": 4664,
            "line_start": 124,
            "line_end": 126
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "- URI scheme: `ftp`\n- Example URI: `ftp://user:pass@ftp.example.com/path/to/export.csv`\n- Required external libraries: none",
        "text_sha256": "e773aeb4b30d92cfb99f0c65195aba80f673ef6ba96cbb8921734bfa6cdbb89d",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 4666,
            "end": 4789,
            "line_start": 128,
            "line_end": 130
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "FTP supports two different connection modes: [active or passive](https://stackoverflow.com/a/1699163). Scrapy uses the passive connection\nmode by default. To use the active connection mode instead, set the\n`FEED_STORAGE_FTP_ACTIVE` setting to `True`.",
        "text_sha256": "4fff04635da16060a45cc8565b94c9581de5067ecc60f61fb5b1562b4ec615c8",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 4791,
            "end": 5041,
            "line_start": 132,
            "line_end": 134
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "http": 10,
    "window_ordinal": 9,
    "window_id": "ff86eff1-17e3-5955-a7b4-7141bc1622cc",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "S3\nThe feeds are stored on [Amazon S3](https://aws.amazon.com/s3/).",
        "text_sha256": "64a8a954ed9fd49c79b7a24731826eb56d380ef49775385d3d4e337e2118fd3e",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 5283,
            "end": 5351,
            "line_start": 144,
            "line_end": 146
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "- URI scheme: `s3`\n- Example URIs:\n  - `s3://mybucket/path/to/export.csv`\n  - `s3://aws_key:aws_secret@mybucket/path/to/export.csv`\n- Required external libraries: [boto3](https://github.com/boto/boto3) >= 1.20.0",
        "text_sha256": "5491f09b951cd467c880f0838f2f3bade0931ae4476b0f6a5cd21fc42d40be84",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 5353,
            "end": 5564,
            "line_start": 148,
            "line_end": 152
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The AWS credentials can be passed as user/password in the URI, or they can be\npassed through the following settings:",
        "text_sha256": "518cd961d6bb479978b5c0c4d8560a9aae3f2a8f2af05a0d0cf4587ba7640dfa",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 5566,
            "end": 5682,
            "line_start": 154,
            "line_end": 155
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "http": 11,
    "window_ordinal": 10,
    "window_id": "65f97431-97f2-51aa-b69b-1dd016d82ff3",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "The AWS credentials can be passed as user/password in the URI, or they can be\npassed through the following settings:",
        "text_sha256": "518cd961d6bb479978b5c0c4d8560a9aae3f2a8f2af05a0d0cf4587ba7640dfa",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 5566,
            "end": 5682,
            "line_start": 154,
            "line_end": 155
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "- [`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`](settings.html#std-setting-AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID)\n- [`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`](settings.html#std-setting-AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY)\n- [`AWS_SESSION_TOKEN`](settings.html#std-setting-AWS_SESSION_TOKEN) (only needed for [temporary security credentials](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/security-creds.html))",
        "text_sha256": "fccefdd0fd1f2f0861b8bb01d6d3dbbaea8663d683450c623216c07a653ebc45",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 5684,
            "end": 6019,
            "line_start": 157,
            "line_end": 159
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "You can also define a custom ACL, custom endpoint, and region name for exported\nfeeds using these settings:",
        "text_sha256": "da6602789e9b34b7f2d815d19619f3ee265b259ef09e44de31c441e2e121e98b",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 6021,
            "end": 6128,
            "line_start": 161,
            "line_end": 162
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "http": 12,
    "window_ordinal": 11,
    "window_id": "2a9d9471-676c-5bc4-8550-ee4b91f1b7ce",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "text": "You can also define a custom ACL, custom endpoint, and region name for exported\nfeeds using these settings:",
        "text_sha256": "da6602789e9b34b7f2d815d19619f3ee265b259ef09e44de31c441e2e121e98b",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 6021,
            "end": 6128,
            "line_start": 161,
            "line_end": 162
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "- `FEED_STORAGE_S3_ACL`\n- [`AWS_ENDPOINT_URL`](settings.html#std-setting-AWS_ENDPOINT_URL)\n- [`AWS_REGION_NAME`](settings.html#std-setting-AWS_REGION_NAME)",
        "text_sha256": "426dace5fa4a5a9f7f44552ec0dd79eafa8ca758bd738abbf518275196994763",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
            "start": 6130,
            "end": 6285,
            "line_start": 164,
            "line_end": 166
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The default value for the `overwrite` key in the `FEEDS` for this\nstorage backend is: `True`.",
        "text_sha256": "5ccc433c6149c1d9a04d58ac240076184ce1c50ba918f1045673e44c93c7fa0f",
        "source_candidates": [
          {
